## Headless implications

- Map CMS field slugs exactly when typing API responses or building fetch layers.
- `sold-out` is a CMS switch, not inventory tracking — headless checkout must respect it.
- Gallery layout uses per-item `column-start` / `column-end` / `list-column-start`. Shop thumbs expose those as attributes `gallery-column-start`, `gallery-column-end`, `list-column`.
- No registered site scripts in Webflow; custom logic lives in this repo.
